WEBVTT

00:10.791 --> 00:17.791
950 YEARS HAVE PASSED
SINCE THE APPEARANCE OF THE FIRST SAMURAI

00:18.541 --> 00:25.541
WITH ONE BATTLE,
THEY VANISHED FROM HISTORY

00:41.041 --> 00:43.166
Charge!

00:45.500 --> 00:46.500
Charge!

02:00.541 --> 02:01.875
It's over!

02:01.958 --> 02:03.791
Raise the cry of victory!

02:05.291 --> 02:07.583
Send up the smoke signal!

02:21.583 --> 02:22.541
What was that?

02:22.625 --> 02:24.000
What's happening?

02:25.083 --> 02:27.041
Enough! It's over!

02:27.125 --> 02:29.583
It's already over! Cease fire!

02:52.208 --> 02:53.291
Stop…

02:53.375 --> 02:54.666
Enough!

02:56.833 --> 03:00.416
Stop!

04:38.958 --> 04:39.833
Shino.

04:40.875 --> 04:43.541
-Let me take over.
-I didn't mean to wake you.

04:46.958 --> 04:49.041
Toya, get me a hand towel.

04:49.125 --> 04:50.041
Okay.

04:54.291 --> 04:55.208
Here.

05:00.333 --> 05:01.750
Father…

05:04.250 --> 05:05.708
It hurts.

05:08.083 --> 05:08.916
Rin.

05:09.708 --> 05:12.500
It's going to be okay.
You'll feel better soon.

05:14.541 --> 05:20.500
I'm sorry. I tried not to catch it.

05:21.500 --> 05:22.875
Don't blame yourself.

05:26.666 --> 05:27.666
Thank you.

05:38.125 --> 05:42.166
FUCHU, KANAGAWA

06:28.833 --> 06:30.666
Enough! It's over!

06:30.750 --> 06:35.541
It's already over! Cease fire!

06:55.666 --> 06:59.041
Ten years since the Boshin War.

06:59.125 --> 07:04.125
Under the new government's modernization
policies, samurai became "Shizoku,"

07:04.208 --> 07:07.833
stripping them
of their privileges and employment.

07:07.916 --> 07:14.916
Meanwhile, lives were devastated
by a widespread outbreak of Cholera.

07:25.833 --> 07:28.625
Mama!

07:34.708 --> 07:35.958
Mr. Saga.

07:36.041 --> 07:39.916
You keep bringing me worthless things.
What am I supposed to do with them?

07:40.541 --> 07:43.500
Forgive me, but please--

07:43.583 --> 07:45.083
Don't do this to me.

07:45.666 --> 07:48.166
It's already been two years
since the Sword Abolishment Edict.

07:48.833 --> 07:51.958
You know the days
of the sword are long gone.

07:55.291 --> 07:58.333
Mr. Saga, don't make this more difficult.

07:58.416 --> 07:59.666
I'll take any price.

08:00.875 --> 08:04.333
Once the cholera passes,
I'll repay your kindness. I swear it.

08:04.416 --> 08:08.000
So please, I'm begging you.

08:13.541 --> 08:15.625
Shino and Rin…

08:17.041 --> 08:18.166
Is it really that bad?

08:27.458 --> 08:30.458
Go and fetch some sugar and salt for him.

08:30.958 --> 08:31.791
Of course.

08:36.291 --> 08:37.791
I don't need your sword.

08:38.666 --> 08:39.833
Take it back with you.

08:42.333 --> 08:43.500
Thank you.

08:46.041 --> 08:47.666
What a time we're living in.

08:50.166 --> 08:52.625
How did things end up like this?

08:57.916 --> 08:59.291
It wasn't there yesterday.

08:59.375 --> 09:03.500
PAWN SHOP

09:03.583 --> 09:04.791
It says it's in Kyoto.

09:05.291 --> 09:07.375
"The opportunity to win 100,000 yen."

09:07.458 --> 09:10.541
-A hundred thousand yen?
-What nonsense.

09:10.625 --> 09:12.125
Can it be real?

09:12.208 --> 09:14.666
No way a martial arts tournament
would pay 100,000 yen.

09:14.750 --> 09:17.166
Still, 100,000 yen? That's…

09:18.000 --> 09:19.916
Enough for ten generations
to live in luxury.

09:21.500 --> 09:24.250
A martial arts tournament, huh?

09:25.291 --> 09:26.500
-Hey, gimme one.
-Me too.

09:26.583 --> 09:29.208
PARTICIPANTS WANTED
ASSEMBLE AT TENRYUJI TEMPLE IN KYOTO

09:29.291 --> 09:31.458
"Those who excel in the martial arts."

09:31.541 --> 09:32.708
"Tenryuji Temple."

09:33.333 --> 09:37.166
"A hundred thousand yen."

09:38.958 --> 09:41.500
This is no ordinary
martial arts tournament.

09:41.583 --> 09:43.416
I wonder.

09:44.000 --> 09:44.833
Hey!

09:44.916 --> 09:45.916
What's going on?

09:46.000 --> 09:47.625
What's the problem?

09:47.708 --> 09:49.875
-Nothing to see here.
-Hey, what is this?

09:49.958 --> 09:51.625
Can we really win 100,000 yen?

09:51.708 --> 09:52.625
How does it work?

09:52.708 --> 09:54.125
-No concern of yours.
-Hand it over.

09:54.208 --> 09:56.000
You're just as guilty for taking it!

10:03.375 --> 10:04.208
Rin!

10:05.250 --> 10:06.250
Rin!

10:08.458 --> 10:10.833
Rin!

10:10.916 --> 10:13.375
-Rin!
-Rin!

10:14.000 --> 10:15.458
Rin!

10:15.958 --> 10:18.958
Rin!

10:22.750 --> 10:24.208
Father…

10:28.000 --> 10:34.791
I couldn't protect Mother and Toya.

10:37.458 --> 10:39.125
I'm sorry.

10:42.791 --> 10:44.083
Rin!

10:45.000 --> 10:46.041
Rin!

10:47.291 --> 10:48.333
Rin…

10:50.125 --> 10:51.125
Rin…

11:09.791 --> 11:11.333
Forgive me.

12:35.375 --> 12:41.750
ASSEMBLE AT TENRYUJI TEMPLE IN KYOTO
AT MIDNIGHT ON MAY 5TH

13:21.916 --> 13:23.458
Shujiro?

13:26.416 --> 13:27.458
Shino.

13:28.916 --> 13:32.541
I'm sorry, but I'll be gone for a while.

13:33.125 --> 13:35.375
I've found a job
that could bring in some money.

13:41.750 --> 13:47.708
With this money, I can save you
and everyone in the village.

13:52.666 --> 13:56.083
Will you draw your sword again?

13:58.541 --> 13:59.833
I wouldn't do that.

14:01.125 --> 14:02.500
Don't worry.

14:15.625 --> 14:17.083
Please stay safe.

14:28.208 --> 14:29.666
I promise I'll return.

14:32.750 --> 14:33.583
I know.

15:17.583 --> 15:22.000
KYOTO

15:23.166 --> 15:24.791
Yes, come in!

15:24.875 --> 15:27.791
Flowers for sale!

15:27.875 --> 15:32.208
Flowers for sale!

15:33.208 --> 15:36.666
-Flowers for sale!
-Get them while they last!

15:43.708 --> 15:45.541
That thing in the newspaper is tonight?

15:45.625 --> 15:49.041
Yeah. I heard it's part
of a government sword hunt.

15:49.125 --> 15:51.083
What is it? Can we go see?

15:51.166 --> 15:53.791
It's not safe. Don't you go near
Tenryuji Temple today.

15:53.875 --> 15:55.125
Why not?

16:06.708 --> 16:08.041
Welcome.

16:08.125 --> 16:08.958
Come in.

16:13.916 --> 16:14.916
Sir Saga?

16:15.000 --> 16:18.250
Yahei, it's been a long time.

16:18.750 --> 16:20.291
A long time, indeed.

16:22.625 --> 16:23.750
I don't suppose…

16:24.333 --> 16:26.083
You too?

16:26.166 --> 16:27.708
Are there others like me?

16:27.791 --> 16:28.750
Yes.

16:29.458 --> 16:34.750
We've had a few guests of a similar sort.

16:37.708 --> 16:39.541
Do you know anything?

16:40.625 --> 16:43.500
Survivors of the old shogunate forces

16:43.583 --> 16:47.125
are gathering comrades, seeking revenge.

16:47.208 --> 16:50.875
But they're just rumors.
I can't be certain.

16:52.791 --> 16:53.958
I see.

17:23.625 --> 17:26.041
Mr. Saga… May I?

17:27.541 --> 17:28.458
Come in.

17:35.833 --> 17:37.750
You're going, then?

17:38.500 --> 17:39.333
Yes.

17:40.583 --> 17:44.750
Kyoto somehow feels different tonight.

17:46.250 --> 17:48.333
Just like in those days,

17:50.125 --> 17:52.916
there's a stench of blood in the air.

17:55.375 --> 17:57.041
Please be careful.

18:10.791 --> 18:15.125
TENRYUJI TEMPLE

18:17.875 --> 18:19.041
Someone's here.

18:34.708 --> 18:36.583
Are you here to participate?

18:38.958 --> 18:39.958
Open the gate.

18:51.250 --> 18:52.250
You may enter.

20:23.166 --> 20:26.125
Man, this is a mess.

20:33.125 --> 20:35.500
They're blinded by fortune.

20:35.583 --> 20:38.625
They might start fighting
before this thing even starts.

20:41.166 --> 20:42.791
Oh, forgive me.

20:43.291 --> 20:46.083
I talk too much when I get nervous.

20:48.125 --> 20:52.583
I'm a former samurai of the Kaga domain.
Kouemon Tachikawa.

20:52.666 --> 20:54.458
The Kaga domain?

20:55.041 --> 20:57.375
The newspaper made it
all the way to Kanazawa?

20:57.458 --> 21:01.541
I asked around about that today.

21:02.041 --> 21:06.083
Seems it was distributed countrywide,
from Hokkaido to Ryukyu.

21:06.166 --> 21:09.875
To go to so much effort…

21:10.750 --> 21:15.250
Perhaps there's some truth
to the 100,000 yen after all.

22:09.625 --> 22:11.250
It is time.

22:11.750 --> 22:14.625
We shall now begin.

22:16.125 --> 22:20.416
First of all, thank you all
for assembling here today.

22:21.041 --> 22:24.625
My name is Enju.

22:30.000 --> 22:31.250
You are about to compete--

22:31.333 --> 22:33.833
or rather, play a game,

22:34.416 --> 22:36.666
that will challenge
your mind, skill, and body.

22:40.541 --> 22:41.666
Of course,

22:41.750 --> 22:44.458
you may doubt the promise
of great wealth from a game.

22:44.541 --> 22:49.583
You may question if such a sum
as large as 100,000 yen truly exists.

23:05.541 --> 23:06.666
What's that jar?

23:18.625 --> 23:22.250
With this much gold,
you could live in luxury for a decade.

23:22.750 --> 23:25.708
But the amount you will win

23:27.416 --> 23:28.666
far surpasses this.

23:38.083 --> 23:40.833
The question is,
how do you obtain such a sum?

23:40.916 --> 23:42.125
But wait.

23:42.708 --> 23:43.791
The thing is,

23:44.666 --> 23:46.625
once you hear the means,

23:47.500 --> 23:50.958
you cannot withdraw from the game
under any circumstances.

23:52.333 --> 23:53.208
What do you mean?

23:55.958 --> 23:58.458
Now, I'm going to count down from 30.

23:58.958 --> 24:01.750
If you no longer wish to participate,

24:02.250 --> 24:04.791
please leave before I finish counting.

24:06.458 --> 24:07.833
Thirty.

24:07.916 --> 24:08.750
Twenty-nine.

24:09.958 --> 24:10.791
Twenty-eight.

24:11.875 --> 24:12.875
Twenty-seven.

24:12.958 --> 24:14.583
-I'm not quitting now!
-Twenty-six.

24:14.666 --> 24:16.250
Twenty-five.

24:16.750 --> 24:18.250
That's enough.

24:32.500 --> 24:33.875
Stay where you are.

24:34.958 --> 24:37.458
I'm Ando from the
Kyoto Prefectural Police, Division Four.

24:38.708 --> 24:40.083
An-Jin the Rushing Gust.

24:43.250 --> 24:45.750
The Fourth Division?

24:46.291 --> 24:50.541
But since you're standing here,
you are a participant as well.

24:51.041 --> 24:53.000
Seems you don't know who I am.

24:53.083 --> 24:55.541
Of course I know you,
An-Jin the Rushing Gust.

24:56.041 --> 24:57.666
Had you been born earlier,

24:57.750 --> 25:00.541
the manslayers and Shinsengumi
wouldn't have stood a chance.

25:00.625 --> 25:03.333
Or so you boldly claim.

25:03.416 --> 25:05.000
It's the truth.

25:05.666 --> 25:08.416
I'm arresting you for violating
the Sword Abolishment Edict.

25:09.250 --> 25:12.166
Don't be so serious. It's just a game.

25:12.250 --> 25:14.166
Who's the organizer? Where are they?

25:15.250 --> 25:16.208
No idea.

25:17.125 --> 25:20.333
Put your hands out. Or I'll cut you down.

25:22.041 --> 25:25.916
So, you won't be participating?

25:26.708 --> 25:30.208
Well, that's too bad.

25:31.625 --> 25:32.791
Cut the crap.

25:55.583 --> 25:58.916
My apologies for the interruption.

26:01.375 --> 26:05.166
I shall resume counting.

26:10.458 --> 26:11.416
Twenty-four.

26:12.666 --> 26:14.000
Twenty-three.

26:14.708 --> 26:15.750
Twenty-two.

26:15.833 --> 26:17.666
-I'm not turning back now.
-Twenty-one.

26:17.750 --> 26:19.291
-This is bad.
-Twenty.

26:20.333 --> 26:21.583
Nineteen.

26:21.666 --> 26:23.500
-Are you going to stay?
-Eighteen.

26:23.583 --> 26:25.125
-I can't do this!
-Seventeen.

26:25.208 --> 26:27.125
-Don't give up now!
-Sixteen.

26:27.208 --> 26:28.958
-I'm going to play!
-Fifteen.

26:29.041 --> 26:30.041
Me too!

26:30.125 --> 26:32.458
-Fourteen.
-If I give up now and go home…

26:32.541 --> 26:34.166
-Thirteen.
-It's for the money!

26:34.250 --> 26:35.166
Twelve.

26:36.250 --> 26:37.375
Eleven.

26:38.083 --> 26:38.958
Ten.

26:39.750 --> 26:41.291
Nine.

26:41.375 --> 26:42.291
Eight.

26:43.291 --> 26:44.291
Seven.

26:45.250 --> 26:46.583
Six.

26:46.666 --> 26:47.666
Five.

26:48.583 --> 26:49.416
Four.

26:51.625 --> 26:53.541
Three, two, one.

26:55.375 --> 26:56.625
Excellent.

26:58.083 --> 27:01.625
Your courage is truly admirable.

27:26.875 --> 27:30.250
MAP OF TOKAIDO ROAD
TENRYUJI TEMPLE

27:30.833 --> 27:34.500
The game you are
about to participate in is called

27:35.250 --> 27:36.250
"Kodoku."

27:36.750 --> 27:40.500
And every game comes with rules.

27:41.375 --> 27:42.750
Write your name on this.

27:42.833 --> 27:44.291
Your name, please.

27:44.375 --> 27:47.083
I shall now explain the rules in detail.

27:47.666 --> 27:48.750
Wear this around your neck.

27:51.750 --> 27:52.666
Rule one.

27:52.750 --> 27:56.333
Your destination is Tokyo.

27:57.291 --> 27:58.291
Rule two.

27:59.083 --> 28:01.000
This is Tenryuji Temple's main gate.

28:01.791 --> 28:03.000
Seki, Ise Province.

28:04.000 --> 28:05.375
Chiryu, Mikawa Province.

28:05.875 --> 28:07.583
Hamamatsu, Totoumi Province.

28:08.083 --> 28:09.750
Shimada, Suruga Province.

28:10.250 --> 28:11.875
Hakone, Sagami Province.

28:12.375 --> 28:13.958
Shinagawa, Musashi Province.

28:14.750 --> 28:17.791
You must pass through
all seven checkpoints.

28:18.583 --> 28:19.958
Write your name.

28:20.041 --> 28:21.416
Wear the wooden tag.

28:23.083 --> 28:24.291
Rule three.

28:24.791 --> 28:27.083
If you do not have enough points,

28:27.583 --> 28:29.666
you cannot proceed to the next town.

28:30.166 --> 28:31.791
Wear this around your neck.

28:31.875 --> 28:32.958
Rule four.

28:34.125 --> 28:37.083
You must not speak
of this game to anyone.

28:38.750 --> 28:40.166
Rule five.

28:40.750 --> 28:43.083
You must arrive in Tokyo

28:43.166 --> 28:45.458
no later than June 5th,
one month from today.

28:46.208 --> 28:47.208
Rule six.

28:47.833 --> 28:50.291
Withdrawing from the game is forbidden.

28:50.375 --> 28:56.083
If your wooden tag is removed
from your neck for ten counts,

28:56.875 --> 28:59.250
it will be considered a withdrawal.

29:02.750 --> 29:03.958
Rule seven.

29:04.541 --> 29:06.291
Anyone who breaks the rules--

29:08.833 --> 29:09.750
Get me outta here!

29:13.541 --> 29:14.958
Ten.

29:15.041 --> 29:16.625
Nine.

29:16.708 --> 29:17.541
Eight.

29:17.625 --> 29:18.875
Seven.

29:19.750 --> 29:21.000
Six.

29:21.083 --> 29:21.958
Five.

29:22.833 --> 29:24.291
-Four.
-Open the gate!

29:24.375 --> 29:25.708
Three.

29:25.791 --> 29:26.791
Two.

29:27.625 --> 29:28.666
One.

29:48.541 --> 29:49.791
Rule seven.

29:51.750 --> 29:56.666
Anyone who breaks the rules
will be punished accordingly.

30:02.541 --> 30:03.791
This is madness.

30:08.166 --> 30:10.708
Nobody said anything about getting killed!

30:24.250 --> 30:26.208
Silence!

30:29.708 --> 30:33.208
Did I not confirm
your intent to participate?

30:34.250 --> 30:40.041
You all chose to join this game
of your own free will.

30:42.083 --> 30:43.750
For 100,000 yen.

30:52.833 --> 30:57.416
Once again, 292 people
have gathered here today.

30:57.500 --> 31:00.791
Each of you has been given a wooden tag
that is worth one point.

31:00.875 --> 31:03.083
Which means each of you
already has one point.

31:05.125 --> 31:09.708
To pass through Tenryuji Temple,
you need at least two points.

31:11.250 --> 31:17.291
And you'll need thirty points
at the final checkpoint, Tokyo.

31:18.875 --> 31:20.833
So, how do you earn points?

31:28.208 --> 31:30.375
Seems some of you already understand.

31:31.875 --> 31:34.166
This can't be real. Is he serious?

31:39.833 --> 31:41.583
You may use any means necessary.

31:42.458 --> 31:44.416
A fight for the wooden tags.

31:59.083 --> 32:04.916
I see many among you who survived
the age of turmoil as samurai.

32:05.000 --> 32:09.541
You are precisely the ones who deserve
the right to claim this fortune.

32:10.958 --> 32:17.333
I ask that you demonstrate
the pride and strength of the samurai.

32:21.958 --> 32:24.416
Should we team up?

32:24.958 --> 32:27.458
Some of these guys
are here with their buddies.

32:27.541 --> 32:29.333
Better than going solo, right?

32:29.416 --> 32:32.583
Besides, I'm pretty good with a sword.

32:33.333 --> 32:35.833
After ten counts,

32:36.833 --> 32:38.250
the game will begin.

32:46.416 --> 32:48.791
Why is there a child here?

32:49.458 --> 32:50.375
Ten.

32:52.375 --> 32:53.333
Nine.

32:55.416 --> 32:56.458
Eight.

32:57.625 --> 32:58.583
Seven.

32:59.958 --> 33:00.875
Six.

33:01.916 --> 33:03.208
Five.

33:04.208 --> 33:05.416
Four.

33:05.500 --> 33:06.666
Three.

33:08.041 --> 33:09.083
Two.

33:10.250 --> 33:11.416
One.

33:17.333 --> 33:19.750
I shall be waiting for you in Tokyo.

33:20.791 --> 33:21.958
Or rather…

33:27.125 --> 33:32.291
In Edo, the city that vanished long ago.

33:43.166 --> 33:44.791
Let the game begin!

33:54.791 --> 33:55.791
Come on!

34:00.708 --> 34:02.208
That's one point for me.

35:55.500 --> 35:56.541
Die!

36:25.291 --> 36:26.458
Hey!

36:36.833 --> 36:37.833
Die!

36:49.041 --> 36:49.916
Sakura.

36:52.083 --> 36:55.458
Does it bring back memories?
Of the old days?

36:57.666 --> 36:58.500
No.

37:10.833 --> 37:12.208
Congratulations.

37:12.875 --> 37:14.291
Show me your wooden tags.

37:19.000 --> 37:20.583
Ukyo Kikuomi.

37:21.375 --> 37:22.833
You're the first.

37:23.583 --> 37:26.000
No wonder they call you
the "Guardian God of the Court Nobles."

37:26.625 --> 37:28.083
What's the point of all this--

37:28.166 --> 37:31.000
I'll be waiting for you in Tokyo.

37:36.750 --> 37:38.125
Confirmed.

37:38.708 --> 37:39.583
Well then…

37:40.583 --> 37:41.875
Safe journey.

37:58.166 --> 37:59.333
Father!

38:09.416 --> 38:12.541
I, um… Thank you, sir.

38:12.625 --> 38:14.083
Do you intend to survive?

38:16.708 --> 38:17.791
I want to live.

38:18.500 --> 38:20.583
I want to live so I can save my mother.

38:22.666 --> 38:24.791
I'll keep you safe
until we get out of here.

38:24.875 --> 38:26.208
Don't leave my side.

38:26.708 --> 38:27.541
I won't.

38:27.625 --> 38:30.333
Hey, he's got a kid! Stop there!

38:30.416 --> 38:31.333
Let's go.

38:47.416 --> 38:48.500
I got one!

39:12.666 --> 39:13.791
Over there!

39:25.666 --> 39:26.958
It's mine!

39:28.000 --> 39:28.875
Give it back!

39:28.958 --> 39:30.416
-Yes!
-Give it to me!

39:30.500 --> 39:31.541
-Ten.
-Give it back!

39:32.541 --> 39:33.625
Nine.

39:35.000 --> 39:36.041
Eight.

39:36.833 --> 39:38.166
Seven.

39:38.958 --> 39:40.208
Six.

39:40.291 --> 39:41.583
Give it!

39:41.666 --> 39:42.583
Five.

39:43.875 --> 39:45.083
Four.

39:46.041 --> 39:47.208
Three.

39:47.916 --> 39:49.208
Two.

39:49.750 --> 39:50.833
One.

39:52.333 --> 39:53.750
120

40:10.500 --> 40:11.333
Grab on.

40:11.416 --> 40:12.416
That's my tag!

40:18.041 --> 40:19.208
Hang on!

40:21.583 --> 40:22.500
Give it!

41:07.166 --> 41:08.083
Let's move.

41:22.750 --> 41:25.875
So it's not you either.

42:14.833 --> 42:16.083
Excuse me.

42:18.916 --> 42:20.958
We have our first to make it through.

42:23.875 --> 42:27.250
Number 19, Ukyo Kikuomi.

42:29.291 --> 42:33.083
He's truly living up to the name,
"Guardian God of the Court Nobles."

42:33.166 --> 42:34.750
"Former" Guardian, I believe.

42:34.833 --> 42:36.250
Seems he's been through a lot.

42:36.333 --> 42:40.083
Still, his swordsmanship is impressive.

42:40.166 --> 42:43.291
Definitely a performance worth watching.

42:43.375 --> 42:45.583
Well, this is just the beginning.

42:46.208 --> 42:48.416
The real entertainment is yet to come.

42:58.208 --> 42:59.250
This way.

43:11.250 --> 43:12.791
What is your name?

43:14.333 --> 43:16.708
Futaba Katsuki. And you, sir?

43:17.208 --> 43:18.541
Shujiro Saga.

43:22.125 --> 43:23.375
What?

43:23.458 --> 43:25.375
Now you just need to make it to the gate.

43:25.458 --> 43:27.000
Wait, what about your wooden tag?

44:21.333 --> 44:23.750
Now, now, calm down.

44:23.833 --> 44:25.833
I've got no intention of fighting you.

44:26.416 --> 44:27.958
I'm just going to pick it up.

44:28.041 --> 44:31.041
Don't come slashing at me out of nowhere.

44:41.916 --> 44:44.208
Here. Take it.

44:47.541 --> 44:49.208
What do you want?

44:50.375 --> 44:52.583
Why are you holding back?

44:53.083 --> 44:55.333
"Kokushu the Manslayer."

45:02.125 --> 45:04.208
Something psychological?

45:06.208 --> 45:08.916
Insomnia. Heart pounding. Shaky hands…

45:09.000 --> 45:13.958
Plenty lost their minds
after the Boshin War.

45:15.333 --> 45:18.791
But if you're planning
to survive with that little miss,

45:18.875 --> 45:20.583
you'd better start killing.

45:24.166 --> 45:26.833
Well, it's up to you.

45:28.083 --> 45:28.916
Wait.

45:32.583 --> 45:34.041
Thank you.

45:36.750 --> 45:39.333
Hang in there. I'm rooting for you.

45:47.125 --> 45:47.958
254

45:52.500 --> 45:54.208
We're running straight to the gate.

45:55.458 --> 45:56.458
Okay.

46:37.166 --> 46:38.916
You go first. Hurry!

46:40.541 --> 46:41.666
Go!

47:41.833 --> 47:43.083
You bastard.

47:48.583 --> 47:49.458
Bastard!

48:27.208 --> 48:30.833
Well done.
Please show me your wooden tags.

48:44.625 --> 48:46.166
Thank you for helping me.

48:46.958 --> 48:49.791
We're going to a friend's inn. Stay alert.

48:51.708 --> 48:52.750
Confirmed.

48:56.833 --> 48:58.083
Safe journey.

49:38.375 --> 49:40.125
It's started to rain.

49:41.625 --> 49:43.500
It certainly has.

49:45.833 --> 49:47.833
Number 108, Shujiro Saga,

49:47.916 --> 49:51.208
and number 120, Futaba Katsuki,
have made it through.

49:52.125 --> 49:56.166
Shujiro Saga,
the Kokushu the Manslayer, huh?

49:56.708 --> 49:58.916
With a child in tow.

49:59.458 --> 50:01.666
Now this is getting interesting!

50:03.916 --> 50:06.125
May I have a moment
of your time, everyone?

50:06.208 --> 50:08.750
What is it? It was just getting good.

50:09.541 --> 50:12.291
A letter from the organizer has arrived.

50:17.291 --> 50:19.291
Allow me to read it for you.

50:23.041 --> 50:29.750
"To all who have agreed to this Kodoku,
I extend my deepest gratitude."

50:31.083 --> 50:36.750
"The samurai are capable
of nothing but swinging swords."

50:38.416 --> 50:43.666
"They mistook privilege for strength."

50:44.708 --> 50:48.458
"They remain blind to the truth
that the world has moved on without them."

50:49.375 --> 50:53.250
"They live on in vain
as fools who have lost all meaning."

50:54.875 --> 51:00.958
"Now let us enjoy this game
and bring ruin to the ghosts

51:01.791 --> 51:05.916
who still call themselves samurai."

51:18.416 --> 51:19.750
Stop!

51:33.583 --> 51:37.458
It's been a while, hasn't it, Kokushu?

51:38.708 --> 51:40.416
Bukotsu Kanjiya.

51:40.916 --> 51:43.291
Has it been ten years?

51:44.250 --> 51:46.333
I've wanted to see you all this time.

51:47.000 --> 51:49.166
I thought I would find you if I came here.

51:53.583 --> 51:54.750
Come on…

51:58.833 --> 52:01.875
Kokushu the Manslayer!

52:19.208 --> 52:23.291
128 REMAINING

56:34.958 --> 56:38.458
Subtitle translation by: Daisy Savage
